   sig="The Woman Who Did was the most radical New Woman novel of the century and the most discussed book of 1895: its heroine's refusal of marriage, its frank treatment of unmarried motherhood and its tragic ending made it a national scandal, and it remains the central text of the argument over free union in the 1890s.",
