   desc="Published in 1890 and the most sophisticated English collection of ghost stories: four tales in which the supernatural is a fact of place, art and psychology.",
   plot="'Amour Dure' follows a German historian in Italy who falls in love with a Renaissance murderess; 'Dionea' presents a child of Venus who destroys the men who love her; 'Oke of Okehurst' tells of a woman who becomes the double of her husband's ancestress; 'A Wicked Voice' is the confession of a composer haunted by an eighteenth-century castrato.",
   ctx="1887-90: the aesthetic movement, the Italian Renaissance revival, the new psychology of the Society for Psychical Research, and the vogue for the supernatural tale.",
