   ctx="1901: the new science of heredity, the Victorian treatment of the disabled, the aesthetic cult of the beautiful body, and the English reception of Nietzsche.",
   sig="The History of Sir Richard Calmady is a landmark of English fiction about the body and one of the boldest novels of its decade: its frank treatment of disability, sexuality and the right to love made it a scandal and a succès, and it has been recovered as one of the most important English novels about physical difference.",
