   ctx="1883: the Victorian crisis of faith, the Darwinian account of nature, the new interest in spiritual experience, and Jefferies's own tuberculosis.",
   sig="The Story of My Heart is one of the great English spiritual autobiographies and the central text of English nature mysticism: its prose about the earth and the soul influenced Edward Thomas, Henry Williamson and the whole tradition of English nature writing, and it is the most personal and most radical of Jefferies's books.",
